From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): honor sheet distance at zero release velocity

Regression exposes native anchored snapping choosing the nearest anchor at exactly zero velocity, ignoring its positionalThreshold. Apply the configured distance decision for that zero-velocity branch through the same shared ScrollScope animation used by direct and nested sheet flings; preserve native nonzero velocity behavior and the existing frame clock guard. Keep small slow movement restoration and fast-flick tests unchanged in intent. Recognize the platform touch slop before testing post-recognition drag distances. Give actual list fixture cells their full width so placement ownership is observable, and include the real zero-height source prepend-loading slot. Shared list/grid leading geometry uses canScrollBackward at the exact beginning even if index zero has no height. Fix Anikku app adapter flag reference and restore its standalone overflow menu Alignment import; retain original APIs and width.
